.TH KEYLATCH\-SANDBOX 1 "2026-05-17" "keylatch" "Keylatch Manual"
.SH NAME
keylatch\-sandbox \- start an isolated credential environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keylatch sandbox
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkeylatch sandbox\fR launches an isolated shell or process environment where
credential access is strictly mediated via the gateway. All runtime modes in
v1.0.0 prevent raw credential values from reaching the subprocess environment.
.PP
For the strongest subprocess isolation, use \fBkeylatch run\fR with
\fI--runtime gateway_typed\fR (the default). The gateway keeps the raw provider
key inside the \fBkeylatchd\fR process and gives the subprocess only a
short-lived session token.
.SH OPTIONS
No stable flags defined yet. Pass \fB\-\-help\fR to see available options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Security block (LLM session guard prevented execution).
.TP
.B 5
Not yet implemented.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR keylatch (1),
.BR keylatch\-run (1),
.BR keylatch\-proxy (1)
